=== the listing
text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
cursor: 1,1
keys: :nmap x dd<CR>:nnoremap y <lt>C-a><lt>Esc><CR>:imap jk <lt>Esc><CR>:omap w e<CR>:map ,f <lt>Space>a <CR>:map<CR>:map!<CR>
output: yes
--- vim 9.1
expect-text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
expect-cursor: 1,1
expect-mode: normal
expect-output:
     ,f            <Space>a<Space>
  o  w             e
  n  x             dd
  n  y           * <C-A><Esc>
  i  jk            <Esc>

=== the listing orders mappings by their first key, newest first
text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
cursor: 1,1
keys: :nmap ab 1<CR>:nmap aa 2<CR>:nmap ac 3<CR>:nmap <lt>F5> 5<CR>:nmap <lt>Del> 6<CR>:nmap <lt>C-]> 4<CR>:nmap Z 7<CR>:nmap é 8<CR>:nmap<CR>
output: yes
--- vim 9.1
expect-text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
expect-cursor: 1,1
expect-mode: normal
expect-output:
  n  Z             7
  n  ac            3
  n  aa            2
  n  ab            1
  n  <C-]>         4
  n  <Del>         6
  n  <F5>          5
  n  é             8

=== the listing shows special keys as Vim does
text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
cursor: 1,1
keys: :nmap x <lt>Tab><lt>lt>\|<lt>Bar><lt>Bslash><lt>C-v><lt>C-a><lt>NL><lt>S-Tab><CR>:nmap y <lt>Leader>x<lt>LocalLeader><CR>:nmap<CR>
output: yes
--- vim 9.1
expect-text:
  one two three
  four five six
  seven eight nine
  ten eleven twelve
expect-cursor: 1,1
expect-mode: normal
expect-output:
  n  x             <Tab><||\<C-V><C-A><NL><S-Tab>
  n  y             \x\

